Assistant (1) 2026-10-15 10:15:00.578 UTC (+186.0s)

The gear selection rule in shift_gears() (src/torcs_v3_physics.py:302) has been updated for V3.11 to eliminate          
short-shifting and maintain higher engine RPM through and out of corners.                                               
                                                                                                                        
### Key Changes                                                                                                         
                                                                                                                        
1. Target Gear Selection (src/torcs_v3_physics.py (src/torcs_v3_physics.py:328)):                                       
    - Updated from picking the highest gear with $\text{rpm} \ge \text{SHIFT_LOW_RPM}$ to finding the lowest gear in    
      [2..6] whose rpm at the current speed is $\le \text{SHIFT_HIGH_RPM}$ (9000).                                      
    - Upshifts occur only when the current gear exceeds SHIFT_HIGH_RPM.                                                 
    - Downshifts occur when the lower gear's RPM would not exceed SHIFT_HIGH_RPM.                                       
    - If no gear in [2..6] has $\text{rpm} \le 9000$ (e.g. at speeds $> 143\text{ km/h}$), the transmission holds its   
      current gear.                                                                                                     
    - Maintained the standing-start launch override (speedX < 10.0 forces gear 1) and the single step per               
      GEAR_HOLD_TICKS (15 ticks) rate limit.                                                                            
                                                                                                                        
2. Self-Tests (src/torcs_v3_physics.py (src/torcs_v3_physics.py:569)):                                                  
    - Updated Case 9 to assert that at $60\text{ km/h}$, gear selection settles at gear 2 (6834 RPM) instead of         
      short-shifting to gear 3 (5530 RPM).                                                                              
    - Ran python src/torcs_v3_physics.py --selftest — all 10 test cases PASS:                                           
      ```text                                                                                                           
        [PASS] Open road on the RIGHT  → steer < 0  (steer=-0.2798)                                                     
        [PASS] Open road on the LEFT   → steer > 0  (steer=+0.3755)                                                     
        [PASS] Car on the LEFT edge    → steer < 0  (steer=-0.5000)                                                     
        [PASS] Car on the RIGHT edge   → steer > 0  (steer=+0.5000)                                                     
        [PASS] Single ray-flip: filtered steer stays below +0.5 (no bang-bang saturation)  (steer=+0.1159)              
        [PASS] Wall 15 m ahead at 105 km/h → brake > 0  (steer=+0.2183)                                                 
        [PASS] 200 m free → target equals physics formula (target=230.0, expected=230.0)  (steer=+0.0000)               
        [PASS] Standing start (0 km/h, gear 4, rpm 15000) → gear 1 (got 1)  (steer=+0.0000)                             
        [PASS] 60 km/h corner exit → gear 2 (settled gear=2, gear-2 rpm=6834 <= SHIFT_HIGH_RPM 9000)  (steer=+0.0000)   
        [PASS] 200 km/h in 6th → stays 6th (gear=6, gear-6 rpm=12587 > SHIFT_HIGH_RPM 9000, no target → hold)           
      (steer=+0.0000)                                                                                                   
      ```                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                        
